{"t": 197.081, "n": 105, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "Phase 2 is built, and its rows 2.1 to 2.6 are marked in the plan. The four test files passed in one run before I fixed an import-order lint error in `test_segment_binding.py`. After that fix I reran only `test_segment_binding.py` (it passed).\n\nOne call was denied: a no-op `python3 -I -c \"pass\"` I sent by mistake. It had no effect on the work.\n\nARTIFACT phase_note: Ran tests/test_segment_binding.py, test_loop_issue_context.py, test_pause_findings_at_final_exit.py and test_loop_child.py (all passed in one run). After an import-order fix I reran only test_segment_binding.py (passed). ruff on src and the three changed test files found one import-order error in test_segment_binding.py, now fixed; mypy was clean. Deviation: in test_segment_binding.py the fast stand-in run puts two segment exits in the same whole second, so the test shifts the later segments' run.jsonl times (and their findings' segment_started and at) by one hour. This is not the plan's \"4 seconds after\" alone, and it keeps the binding unambiguous. Added test_an_issue_shows_the_pauses_reason_when_no_facts_row_was_made. The helper `check_paused_context` now takes the pause reason and the exit reason. The step-7 spec search found no spec that this change makes false.", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "9249d138-7b65-4cb5-b2c0-f89f3fee3a37"}
